{"name":"Soleil","hex":"#e9cb2e","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"soleil","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["sun"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soleil"}],"entries":[{"title":"Soleil (Jean-Pierre Ferland album)","blocks":[{"text":"Soleil is an album by Jean-Pierre Ferland, released in 1971. It is a double album with as many as 14 songs. Guitarist David Spinozza is featured on the album, he has played on Jean-Pierre Ferland's previous album Jaune which was published in 1970, and he who would also play with Paul and Linda McCartney on their album Ram in 1971."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e1/Soleil%28AlbumCover%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soleil_(Jean-Pierre_Ferland_album)"},{"title":"SOLEIL","blocks":[{"text":"SOLEIL is a synchrotron facility near Paris, France. It performed its first acceleration of electrons on May 14, 2006. The name SOLEIL is a backronym for Source Optimisée de Lumière d’Énergie Intermédiaire du LURE, LURE meaning Laboratoire pour l'Utilisation du Rayonnement Électromagnétique."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/VueAerienneSynchrotronSOLEIL.jpg/330px-VueAerienneSynchrotronSOLEIL.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SOLEIL"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Sch%C3%A9ma_de_principe_du_synchrotron.jpg/500px-Sch%C3%A9ma_de_principe_du_synchrotron.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Sch%C3%A9ma_de_principe_du_synchrotron.jpg/1280px-Sch%C3%A9ma_de_principe_du_synchrotron.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Sch%C3%A9ma_de_principe_du_synchrotron.jpg/500px-Sch%C3%A9ma_de_principe_du_synchrotron.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Diagram of machinery","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASch%C3%A9ma_de_principe_du_synchrotron.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/SynchrotronSoleil-VueInterieur.jpg/500px-SynchrotronSoleil-VueInterieur.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/SynchrotronSoleil-VueInterieur.jpg/1280px-SynchrotronSoleil-VueInterieur.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/SynchrotronSoleil-VueInterieur.jpg/500px-SynchrotronSoleil-VueInterieur.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"View of the interior of facility","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASynchrotronSoleil-VueInterieur.jpg"}],"sounds":{"soleil":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/27/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Flame%2C_not_lame-soleil.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/27/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Flame%2C_not_lame-soleil.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Flame%2C_not_lame-soleil.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/27/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Flame%2C_not_lame-soleil.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Flame%2C_not_lame-soleil.wav.ogg"}]}}}